IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lsl-employee`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, "Which of these describes you"): the employee (the baseline's seat); the employer, on whom the Act
-- puts the duties to grant the leave, pay it out, keep and show the records and pass them on a transfer of business; and
-- the personal representative of an employee who has died, to whom the employer must pay the leave on request
-- (s 9(2A)(b)). Every exported question takes `my role` first. A question about another role answers `does not arise
-- for you` without reading any other input, so the form never asks those inputs. An industrial inspector, the
-- industrial magistrate's court and the Commission are never a seat.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's
-- fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading anything
-- else. The questions of one situation share one input, the same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. All
-- are BOOLEAN, and FALSE gives `does not arise for you`:
--   - for the employee, `my employment has ended`: the entitlement on termination, the weeks and dollars paid out
--     (ss 8(2), (3), 9(2), (2A)) and the deduction for leave taken in advance (s 10(2));
--   - for the employee, `I have had an absence or break in my employment`: continuity and what counts (ss 6, 6A);
--   - for the employee, `I have moved to a new employer`: whether the service carries over (ss 7E-7H, 41);
--   - for the employee, `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave`: the s 9(1C), (1D) options, payment before
--     the leave (s 9(3)), public holidays (s 9(4)) and work during the leave (s 27);
--   - for the employer, `my employee's employment has ended`: the weeks and dollars to pay out and the s 10(2)
--     deduction.
-- No question that arises in every situation of its role takes one. The personal representative's role is itself the
-- situation (the employee died), so its questions take none.
--
-- For the employee, each question calls the baseline function of the same subject in lsl-employee.l4 and restates no
-- rule; where its situation holds its answer is the baseline export's, carried in the answer types below. The employer's
-- and the personal representative's questions call the same functions, asked from their side. No exported question
-- takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am an employee in Western Australia`
    `I employ people in Western Australia`
    `I am the personal representative of an employee who has died`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Weeks answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    weeks HAS `number of weeks` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `this many days` HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Fraction answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `this fraction of your ordinary pay` HAS `fraction` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Years answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `during the employment and for at least this many years after it` HAS `years` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Text answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    text HAS `the answer` IS A STRING

-- ss 7E-7H, 41, carried: the baseline's three answers, worded so either party can read them, and `does not arise for
-- you`.
DECLARE `Service answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the service carries over to the new employer`
    `the service with the new employer starts from zero`
    `the former s 6 decides, as the business was transmitted before 20 June 2022 (s 41)`

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers, and the helpers the other roles need`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A ServiceOutcome
GIVETH A `Service answer`
`the service outcome, carried` `the outcome` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `my service carries over to the new employer` THEN `the service carries over to the new employer`
    WHEN `my service with the new employer starts from zero` THEN `the service with the new employer starts from zero`
    WHEN `the former s 6 decides, as the business was transmitted before 20 June 2022` THEN `the former s 6 decides, as the business was transmitted before 20 June 2022 (s 41)`

-- s 7I(2): "On the transfer of a business, the old employer must transfer copies of all transferring employees'
-- employment records to the new employer." A transfer of business is s 7E's, the test the carry-over function applies;
-- for a business transmitted before 20 June 2022, s 41(2)(b) disapplies Part II Division 3, s 7I with it. Every value
-- is listed, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the outcome` IS A ServiceOutcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a transfer of business under Division 3` IF
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `my service carries over to the new employer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my service with the new employer starts from zero` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the former s 6 decides, as the business was transmitted before 20 June 2022` THEN FALSE

-- s 9(2), (2A)(b): an employee entitled under s 8(2) or (3) whose employment ends before all the leave is taken is taken
-- to start the leave on that day, and the employer must pay the full amount, "if the employee has died -- on request,
-- to the employee's personal representative".
GIVEN `the employee's years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER
      `weeks of long service leave the employee had taken` IS A NUMBER
      `I have asked the employer for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must pay the personal representative` IF
        `I have asked the employer for it`
    AND `How many weeks must I be paid out` `the employee's years of continuous employment` `I died` `weeks of long service leave the employee had taken` GREATER THAN 0

§§ `For the employee (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (lsl-employee.l4) and restates no rule: for this
-- role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `s 4A -- does the Act apply to me`

@export Does the Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) apply to me (ss 4, 4A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed to do work for hire or reward (apprentices, casuals and seasonal workers included)
      `my award, agreement or another law gives me long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, industrial agreement, employer-employee agreement or another Australian law gives you long service leave and payment instead of it on termination
      `what I get instead is only a loading or extra payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you get in place of long service leave is only a loading or other extra payment in your pay
      `if that entitlement is at least equivalent to the Act's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that other entitlement is at least as good as the Act's, both to take leave and to be paid out on termination (a judgment: a court decides it if disputed)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the WA Long Service Leave Act apply to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Does the Act apply to me` `I am an employee` `my award, agreement or another law gives me long service leave` `what I get instead is only a loading or extra payment` `if that entitlement is at least equivalent to the Act's`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 6, 6A -- what counts as continuous employment`

@export Is my employment still continuous after this absence or break (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have had an absence or break in my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with this employer has had an absence, leave, a stand-down, a dismissal and re-employment, or a gap between engagements (s 6)
      `the facts` IS AN AbsenceFacts @desc What the absence was and what happened around it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my employment still continuous after this absence or break` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I have had an absence or break in my employment`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my employment still continuous` `the facts`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does this absence count towards the length of my continuous employment (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 6A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have had an absence or break in my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with this employer has had an absence, leave, a stand-down, a dismissal and re-employment, or a gap between engagements (s 6)
      `the facts` IS AN AbsenceFacts @desc What the absence was and what happened around it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this absence count towards my length of service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I have had an absence or break in my employment`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does this period count towards my service` `the facts`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my apprenticeship count towards my long service leave with this employer (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 6(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I did my apprenticeship with this employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the apprenticeship was with the same employer you now work for
      `weeks from finishing it to my new contract` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks between completing the apprenticeship and entering your contract of employment with that employer
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my apprenticeship count towards my long service leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Does my apprenticeship count` `I did my apprenticeship with this employer` `weeks from finishing it to my new contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7E-7H, 41 -- does my service follow me to a new employer`

@export When I change employer, does my service carry over for long service leave (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 7E-7H, 8(1), 41)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have moved to a new employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with one employer ended and you then became employed by another (ss 7D-7H)
      `the change` IS A ChangeOfEmployer @desc How you moved from the old employer to the new one
GIVETH A `Service answer`
`Does my service carry over to my new employer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I have moved to a new employer`
        THEN `the service outcome, carried` (`Does my service carry over` `the change`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 8 -- how much long service leave have I earned`

@export How many weeks of long service leave have I earned so far while still employed (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 8(2)(a), (b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your years of continuous employment with this employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of long service leave have I earned so far` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN `weeks` (`How many weeks of long service leave have I earned` `years of continuous employment`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to when my employment ends, before any leave taken (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 8(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with this employer has ended, by resignation, dismissal, redundancy or otherwise
      `years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your years of continuous employment with this employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `how it ended` IS A Termination @desc How the employment ended
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of long service leave am I entitled to now my employment has ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `my employment has ended`
        THEN `weeks` (`How many weeks am I entitled to on termination` `years of continuous employment` `how it ended`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many weeks of long service leave must I be paid out when my employment ends (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 8, 9(2), 9(2A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with this employer has ended, by resignation, dismissal, redundancy or otherwise
      `years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your years of continuous employment with this employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `how it ended` IS A Termination @desc How the employment ended
      `weeks of long service leave already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you have already taken or been paid for with this employer
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of long service leave must I be paid out` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `my employment has ended`
        THEN `weeks` (`How many weeks must I be paid out` `years of continuous employment` `how it ended` `weeks of long service leave already taken`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7, 7A, 7B, 7C, 9(2A) -- what is my ordinary pay, and what I am paid out`

@export What is my weekly ordinary pay for long service leave, in dollars (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 7, 7A, 7B, 7C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my pay` IS A PayFacts @desc How you are paid (leave out overtime, shift premiums, penalty rates and allowances)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is my weekly ordinary pay for long service leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN `amount` (`What is my weekly ordinary pay` `my pay`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much must I be paid for long service leave when my employment ends, in dollars (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 8, 9(2A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with this employer has ended, by resignation, dismissal, redundancy or otherwise
      `years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc Your years of continuous employment with this employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `how it ended` IS A Termination @desc How the employment ended
      `weeks of long service leave already taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you have already taken or been paid for with this employer
      `my weekly ordinary pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly ordinary pay in dollars (s 7)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must I be paid for long service leave now my employment has ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `my employment has ended`
        THEN `amount` (`How much must I be paid out` `years of continuous employment` `how it ended` `weeks of long service leave already taken` `my weekly ordinary pay`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 9 -- taking the leave`

@export May I take my long service leave at a time I choose, without my employer's agreement (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 9(1a), (1b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employer and I have agreed when I take it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer have already agreed when you will take the leave
      `months since I became entitled to it` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since you became entitled to this period of leave
      `weeks of notice I give` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of notice you give your employer of the period you intend to take
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I take my long service leave at a time I choose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`May I take my leave when I choose` `my employer and I have agreed when I take it` `months since I became entitled to it` `weeks of notice I give`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If my request for longer leave at half pay, or shorter leave at double pay, is granted, how many weeks of leave do I get (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 9(1C), (1D))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on long service leave, or have arranged or asked to take it, or are taken to have started it when your employment ended (s 9(2))
      `weeks of leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you are entitled to at full pay
      `the mode` IS A LeaveMode @desc Full pay, twice as long at half pay, or half as long at double pay
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of leave do I get if my request is granted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave`
        THEN `weeks` (`How many weeks of leave if granted` `weeks of leave` `the mode`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If my request is granted, what fraction of my ordinary pay am I paid during the leave (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 9(1C), (1D))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on long service leave, or have arranged or asked to take it, or are taken to have started it when your employment ended (s 9(2))
      `the mode` IS A LeaveMode @desc Full pay, twice as long at half pay, or half as long at double pay
GIVETH A `Fraction answer`
`What fraction of my ordinary pay am I paid during my leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave`
        THEN `this fraction of your ordinary pay` (`What fraction of my ordinary pay during leave` `the mode`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be paid for my long service leave before it starts (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 9(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on long service leave, or have arranged or asked to take it, or are taken to have started it when your employment ended (s 9(2))
      `I asked in writing to be paid before the leave starts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked your employer in writing to be paid before the leave begins
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be paid for my leave before it starts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I be paid before my leave starts` `I asked in writing to be paid before the leave starts`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days longer is my long service leave because of public holidays (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 9(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on long service leave, or have arranged or asked to take it, or are taken to have started it when your employment ended (s 9(2))
      `public holidays during my leave that I would otherwise get` IS A NUMBER @desc Public holidays falling in your leave to which your conditions of employment otherwise entitle you
      `the leave is taken under s 8(2)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is leave taken while employed after 10 (or 15, 20 ...) years, not leave paid out on termination
GIVETH A `Days answer`
`How many days longer is my leave because of public holidays` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave`
        THEN `this many days` (`How many days longer is my leave` `public holidays during my leave that I would otherwise get` `the leave is taken under s 8(2)(a) or (b)`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 5, 10, 27 -- cashing out, leave in advance, working during leave`

@export Is my agreement to cash out long service leave valid (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the leave has already accrued under s 8(2)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the leave being cashed out had already accrued (after 10, 15, 20 ... years) when you agreed
      `the agreement is in writing signed by both of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is in writing and signed by you and your employer
      `the amount I am paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars you are paid instead of the leave
      `ordinary pay I would have received for that leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of ordinary pay you would have received had you taken the leave
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my agreement to cash out my long service leave valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is my cash-out agreement valid` `the leave has already accrued under s 8(2)(a) or (b)` `the agreement is in writing signed by both of us` `the amount I am paid` `ordinary pay I would have received for that leave`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many weeks of leave taken in advance can my employer recover from my final pay (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 10(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with this employer has ended, by resignation, dismissal, redundancy or otherwise
      `weeks of leave I took` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you have taken, including any taken in advance
      `weeks I was entitled to when my employment ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you were entitled to on the day the employment ended (s 8)
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of leave taken in advance can my employer recover from my final pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `my employment has ended`
        THEN `weeks` (`How many weeks can my employer deduct` `weeks of leave I took` `weeks I was entitled to when my employment ended`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I forfeit the rest of my long service leave by working for someone else during it (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 27)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on long service leave, or have arranged or asked to take it, or are taken to have started it when your employment ended (s 9(2))
      `I worked for reward in place of my job during the leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while on long service leave, you took paid work in substitution for the job you are on leave from
      `this is leave I was taken to start on termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the leave you are treated as starting on the day your employment ended (s 9(2))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I forfeit the rest of my leave by working elsewhere during it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `I am taking, or about to take, long service leave`
        THEN `yes if` (`Do I forfeit the rest of my leave` `I worked for reward in place of my job during the leave` `this is leave I was taken to start on termination`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 26A -- seeing my records`

@export Must my employer let me see my long service leave records (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 26A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I or someone I authorised in writing asked in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or a person you authorised in writing, asked the employer in writing
      `years since my employment ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Years since your employment with that employer ended (0 if you still work there)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my employer let me see my long service leave records` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Must my employer let me see my records` `I or someone I authorised in writing asked in writing` `years since my employment ended`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must my employer let me see my records (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 26A(3)(d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`By when must my employer let me see my records` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee in Western Australia` THEN `text` (`By when must I be shown my records`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the employer (ss 4A, 5, 6, 6A, 7E-7I, 8, 9, 10, 26, 26A, 27)`

-- The Act puts on the employer the duties to grant the leave (s 9(1), (1a)), to pay it out on termination (s 9(2A)),
-- to keep records for 7 years after the employment (s 26), to let the employee see them (s 26A) and, on a transfer of
-- business, to pass them to the new employer (s 7I). The employee's facts are asked of the employer through the same
-- records and functions as the employee's questions: the record fields keep the employee's first-person wording.

§§§ `s 4A -- does the Act apply to my employee`

@export Does the Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) apply to my employee (ss 4, 4A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person is my employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is employed by you to do work for hire or reward (apprentices, casuals and seasonal workers included)
      `an award, agreement or another law gives the employee long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, industrial agreement, employer-employee agreement or another Australian law gives the employee long service leave and payment instead of it on termination
      `what the employee gets instead is only a loading or extra payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what the employee gets in place of long service leave is only a loading or other extra payment in their pay
      `that entitlement is at least equivalent to the Act's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that other entitlement is at least as good as the Act's, both to take leave and to be paid out on termination (a judgment: a court decides it if disputed)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the Act apply to my employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Does the Act apply to me` `the person is my employee` `an award, agreement or another law gives the employee long service leave` `what the employee gets instead is only a loading or extra payment` `that entitlement is at least equivalent to the Act's`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 6, 6A -- my employee's continuous employment`

@export Is my employee's employment still continuous after this absence or break (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee's absence` IS AN AbsenceFacts @desc What the employee's absence was and what happened around it (the fields are worded from the employee's side)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my employee's employment still continuous after this absence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is my employment still continuous` `the employee's absence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my employee's absence count towards the length of their continuous employment (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 6A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee's absence` IS AN AbsenceFacts @desc What the employee's absence was and what happened around it (the fields are worded from the employee's side)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my employee's absence count towards their length of service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Does this period count towards my service` `the employee's absence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7E-7I, 41 -- transfer of business`

@export Does my employee's service with their old employer count as service with me (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 7E-7H, 41)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the change` IS A ChangeOfEmployer @desc How the employee moved from their old employer to you (the fields are worded from the employee's side)
GIVETH A `Service answer`
`Does my new employee's service with their old employer count with me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `the service outcome, carried` (`Does my service carry over` `the change`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 7I(2) binds the old employer "on the transfer of a business", which is s 7E's: the same test as the carry-over
-- question. For a business transmitted before 20 June 2022, Part II Division 3, s 7I with it, does not apply (s 41(2)(b)).
@export My employees have moved to a new employer: must I transfer copies of their employment records to it (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 7I(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the change` IS A ChangeOfEmployer @desc How the employee moved from you to the new employer (the fields are worded from the employee's side)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I pass my former employees' records to the new employer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`there is a transfer of business under Division 3` (`Does my service carry over` `the change`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 8, 9, 10 -- my employee's leave, and paying it out`

@export How many weeks of long service leave has my employee earned so far (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 8(2)(a), (b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee's years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's years of continuous employment with you, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of long service leave has my employee earned` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN weeks (`How many weeks of long service leave have I earned` `the employee's years of continuous employment`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I let my employee take their long service leave at a time that suits them (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 9(1a), (1b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `we have agreed when the employee takes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the employee have already agreed when the leave will be taken
      `months since the employee became entitled to it` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the employee became entitled to this period of leave
      `weeks of notice the employee gave` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of notice the employee gave you of the period they intend to take
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I let my employee take their leave at the time they choose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`May I take my leave when I choose` `we have agreed when the employee takes it` `months since the employee became entitled to it` `weeks of notice the employee gave`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I pay my employee for their long service leave before it starts (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 9(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee asked in writing to be paid before the leave starts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee asked you in writing to be paid before the leave begins
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I pay my employee for the leave before it starts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Must I be paid before my leave starts` `the employee asked in writing to be paid before the leave starts`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export My employee's employment has ended: how many weeks of long service leave must I pay out (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 8, 9(2), (2A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employee's employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment of the employee you are asking about has ended
      `the employee's years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's years of continuous employment with you, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `how the employment ended` IS A Termination @desc How the employee's employment ended
      `weeks of long service leave the employee has taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave the employee has already taken or been paid for with you
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of long service leave must I pay out to my employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `my employee's employment has ended`
        THEN weeks (`How many weeks must I be paid out` `the employee's years of continuous employment` `how the employment ended` `weeks of long service leave the employee has taken`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export My employee's employment has ended: how much must I pay them for long service leave, in dollars, on the day it ended (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 8, 9(2), (2A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employee's employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment of the employee you are asking about has ended
      `the employee's years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's years of continuous employment with you, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `how the employment ended` IS A Termination @desc How the employee's employment ended
      `weeks of long service leave the employee has taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave the employee has already taken or been paid for with you
      `the employee's weekly ordinary pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's weekly ordinary pay in dollars (s 7)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must I pay my employee for long service leave now their employment has ended` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `my employee's employment has ended`
        THEN amount (`How much must I be paid out` `the employee's years of continuous employment` `how the employment ended` `weeks of long service leave the employee has taken` `the employee's weekly ordinary pay`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export My employee's employment has ended: how many weeks of leave they took in advance may I deduct from their final pay (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 10(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my employee's employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment of the employee you are asking about has ended
      `weeks of leave the employee took` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave the employee has taken, including any taken in advance
      `weeks the employee was entitled to when the employment ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave the employee was entitled to on the day the employment ended (s 8)
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of leave taken in advance may I deduct from my employee's final pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN
        IF `my employee's employment has ended`
        THEN weeks (`How many weeks can my employer deduct` `weeks of leave the employee took` `weeks the employee was entitled to when the employment ended`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 5, 27 -- cashing out, and work during leave`

@export Is my agreement with my employee to cash out their long service leave valid (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the leave has already accrued under s 8(2)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the leave being cashed out had already accrued (after 10, 15, 20 ... years) when you agreed
      `the agreement is in writing signed by both of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is in writing and signed by you and the employee
      `the amount I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars you pay the employee instead of the leave
      `ordinary pay the employee would have received for that leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars of ordinary pay the employee would have received had they taken the leave
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my agreement to cash out my employee's long service leave valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is my cash-out agreement valid` `the leave has already accrued under s 8(2)(a) or (b)` `the agreement is in writing signed by both of us` `the amount I pay` `ordinary pay the employee would have received for that leave`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 27(2): the employee's forfeiture and the employer's right to withhold and reclaim are one consequence.
@export My employee worked elsewhere during long service leave: may I withhold further leave pay and reclaim what I paid for the rest of it (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 27(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee worked for reward in place of their job during the leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while on long service leave, the employee took paid work in substitution for the job they are on leave from
      `this is leave the employee was taken to start on termination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the leave the employee is treated as starting on the day their employment ended (s 9(2))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I withhold or reclaim leave pay from an employee who worked elsewhere during the leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Do I forfeit the rest of my leave` `the employee worked for reward in place of their job during the leave` `this is leave the employee was taken to start on termination`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 26, 26A -- records`

-- s 26 binds every employer, so the answer is settled by the role alone.
@export How long must I keep each employee's long service leave employment records (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 26(1), (2)(b); a civil penalty provision, s 26(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Years answer`
`How long must I keep my employees' long service leave records` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `during the employment and for at least this many years after it` 7
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I let my employee, or someone they authorised, see their long service leave records (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 26A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee or someone they authorised in writing asked in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee, or a person the employee authorised in writing, asked you in writing
      `years since the employment ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Years since the employee's employment with you ended (0 if they still work for you)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I let my employee see their long service leave records` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Must my employer let me see my records` `the employee or someone they authorised in writing asked in writing` `years since the employment ended`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must I let my employee see their records (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) s 26A(3)(d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`By when must I let my employee see their records` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ people in Western Australia` THEN text (`By when must I be shown my records`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the personal representative of an employee who has died (ss 8(2), (3), 9(2), (2A)(b))`

-- s 9(2A)(b): when an employee dies before taking all their leave, the employer must pay "on request, to the
-- employee's personal representative". The questions call the baseline's termination functions with `I died`.

§§§ `ss 8, 9(2), (2A)(b) -- the leave of an employee who died`

@export Must the employer pay me, as personal representative, the long service leave of the employee who died (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 8(2), (3), 9(2), (2A)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee's years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of continuous employment the employee who died had with the employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `weeks of long service leave the employee had taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave the employee had already taken or been paid for with that employer
      `I have asked the employer for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as personal representative, have asked the employer for the payment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the employer pay me the long service leave of the employee who died` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the personal representative of an employee who has died` THEN `yes if` (`the employer must pay the personal representative` `the employee's years of continuous employment` `weeks of long service leave the employee had taken` `I have asked the employer for it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many weeks of long service leave must be paid for the employee who died (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 8(2), (3), 9(2), (2A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee's years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of continuous employment the employee who died had with the employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `weeks of long service leave the employee had taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave the employee had already taken or been paid for with that employer
GIVETH A `Weeks answer`
`How many weeks of long service leave must be paid for the employee who died` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the personal representative of an employee who has died` THEN weeks (`How many weeks must I be paid out` `the employee's years of continuous employment` `I died` `weeks of long service leave the employee had taken`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much must the employer pay me, in dollars, for the long service leave of the employee who died (Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA) ss 8, 9(2A)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employee's years of continuous employment` IS A NUMBER @desc The years of continuous employment the employee who died had with the employer, counted under s 6A (unpaid leave left out)
      `weeks of long service leave the employee had taken` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave the employee had already taken or been paid for with that employer
      `the employee's weekly ordinary pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly ordinary pay, in dollars, of the employee who died (s 7)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much must be paid to me for the long service leave of the employee who died` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the personal representative of an employee who has died` THEN amount (`How much must I be paid out` `the employee's years of continuous employment` `I died` `weeks of long service leave the employee had taken` `the employee's weekly ordinary pay`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
